.TH ZFS-NCDU 1 "2026-09-20" "zfs-ncdu 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zfs\-ncdu \- browse ZFS space accounting in ncdu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zfs\-ncdu
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIdataset\fR|\fIpool\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zfs\-ncdu
renders ZFS dataset, snapshot and reservation accounting into
.BR ncdu (1)'s
JSON export format and opens it with the real
.B ncdu
binary.
.PP
Walking a directory tree cannot measure ZFS. Snapshots hold blocks that no live
file references, compression means on-disk bytes differ from file sizes, and
reservations consume space no file occupies. Those live in dataset properties,
not in the filesystem namespace, so
.BR du (1)
and a plain
.B ncdu
scan of a mountpoint all miss them.
.PP
With no arguments every imported pool is included. Each dataset becomes a
directory contributing no bytes of its own; its space appears as
.IR [data] ,
.IR [refreservation] ,
and a
.I [snapshots]
directory holding one entry per snapshot. Disk size is bytes on disk; apparent
size is the logical size they represent, so ncdu's
.B a
key toggles between compressed and uncompressed views.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-depth " \fIN\fR"
Recurse at most \fIN\fR levels below each argument, as in \fBzfs list \-d\fR.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-no\-snapshots
Summarise snapshots as a single entry per dataset instead of listing each one.
Faster on datasets with very many snapshots.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the export to \fIFILE\fR (\fB\-\fR for standard output) and exit without
starting ncdu. The file can be read later with \fBncdu \-f\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite an existing \fB\-\-output\fR file.
.TP
.BR \-\-privilege " \fICMD\fR"
Command used to reach \fBzfs\fR, for example \fBsudo\fR or \fBdoas\fR, or
\fBnone\fR to require none. By default an unprivileged \fBzfs\fR is tried
first and a privilege helper is only used if that fails.
.TP
.BR \-\-ncdu " \fIPATH\fR"
The ncdu binary to run.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-V ", " \-\-version
Show help or version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZFS_NCDU_AWK
Path to \fIzfs\-ncdu.awk\fR. By default it is found relative to the executable.
.TP
.B ZFS_NCDU_PRIVILEGE
Default for \fB\-\-privilege\fR.
.TP
.B NCDU
Default for \fB\-\-ncdu\fR.
.TP
.B AWK
awk implementation to use.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Where generated exports are cached, \fI~/.cache/zfs\-ncdu\fR by default.
.SH ACCOUNTING NOTES
For every dataset ZFS maintains
.IP
USED = USEDDS + USEDSNAP + USEDREFRESERV + USEDCHILD
.PP
and the generated tree reproduces that identity exactly: the totals ncdu shows
equal the dataset's USED.
.PP
A snapshot's own USED counts only space unique to it. Space held jointly by
two or more snapshots is charged to none of them, so listing snapshots alone
would total less than USEDSNAP. The difference is reported as
.IR "[shared between snapshots]" .
.PP
Pool level figures from \fBzpool list\fR differ from the sum of dataset USED,
because raidz parity, padding and pool metadata are counted there but belong to
no dataset. This tool reports dataset accounting, not pool geometry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Browse every imported pool:
.B zfs\-ncdu
.TP
Browse one dataset and its children:
.B zfs\-ncdu tank/home
.TP
Save an export to read later, without opening ncdu:
.B zfs\-ncdu \-o tank.ncdu tank && ncdu \-f tank.ncdu
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ncdu (1),
.BR zfs (8),
.BR zfs-list (8),
.BR zpool (8)
